test_parity -- del_vor's .stor against LaGriT's dump / stor (Nov 2026)
=======================================================================

QUICK START

  sh run_parity_tests.sh [path-to-del_vor]   14 meshes (15 with the
                                              big one), about 10 s
  open summary.html

WHAT IS TESTED

  For each mesh of cases.txt, LaGriT's dump / stor and del_vor write a
  .stor of the same .inp, and ../../../tools/stor_compare.py compares
  them pair by pair and vertex by vertex. Every difference must have
  an explanation; one that has none fails the case.

  del_vor -avs NAME.inp -stor NAME_keep.stor -zero_area keep -compress off
  del_vor -avs NAME.inp -stor NAME.stor

  compared with LaGriT's files (made once by make_parity_gold.sh, in
  inputs/):

  NAME_lg.stor        dump / stor / NAME_lg / mo   (LaGriT's default:
                      anothermatbld3d in 3D, compressed; matbld2d in
                      2D, uncompressed)
  NAME_lg_none.stor   dump / stor / NAME_lg_none / mo / ascii / none
                      (3D only: matbld3d_stor, uncompressed; LaGriT's 2D
                      writer gives the same file both ways)

  Meshes: lanl/voronoi's three; LaGriT's test_poisson_3d cases 1 and 2
  and the three test_poisson_2d meshes; LaGriT level01 meshes
  (pflotran_stor, io_agf_simple, recon1's fracture network); a
  two-material jittered grid made by LaGriT; poi3d_01 at UTM-size
  coordinates; Carl's dfnWorks 4_user_rects_uniform; and, outside git,
  dfnWorks TPL_nonuniform (57,257 vertices, 114,739 triangles).

WHAT IS CHECKED (check_parity.py)

  exit           both del_vor runs exit 0
  keep_vs_lg     every difference against LaGriT's default explained
  keep_vs_none   the same against LaGriT's uncompressed 3D file
  default_vs_lg  del_vor's defaults against LaGriT's default
  MEASURED       the largest differences, the labels, volume totals

  The labels (defined at the top of tools/stor_compare.py): digits
  (the printed digits: 13 in LaGriT's
  files, 17 in del_vor's), round_off (small values made by
  cancellation, within 64 u of the largest), merge (LaGriT's 1e-8
  compression), zero_area, dropped (LaGriT's rule: coefficients below
  1e-8 of the largest left out) and dropped_share (those pairs' share
  of their vertices' volumes), abs_coords (LaGriT computes 3D tet
  volumes from absolute coordinates), nstor_magnitude (see below).

FOUND IN LAGRIT (not del_vor's; explained, so the cases pass)

  - dump / stor ... / none in 3D (matbld3d_stor.f, header
    matbld3d_nstor) writes |A|/d, the magnitude of the area vector
    (amat = sqrt(xamat**2 + yamat**2 + zamat**2)): every negative
    coefficient comes out positive. poi3d_01: all 75 negative
    coefficients hidden. LaGriT's default writer keeps the sign.
  - At UTM-size coordinates LaGriT's 3D volumes are wrong (utm_tet:
    total -100.5 for a box of volume 0.032; del_vor 0.0319999999944);
    anothermatbld3d's TranslateTetToZero does not translate (reported
    to Carl, notes/lagrit_reports/anothermatbld3d_translate_bug.md).

BIG CASES (outside git)

  A mesh path starting with big/ is in the folder DEL_VOR_BIG
  (default ~/lagrit_work/del_vor_dev/big_inputs); LaGriT's .stor files
  for it are in DEL_VOR_BIG/parity. Without them the case is SKIPPED.
  To make them:

    sh make_parity_gold.sh /path/to/lagrit ~/lagrit_work/del_vor_dev/big_inputs

PICTURES (logs/)

  NAME.svg  the mesh (every edge, or for big meshes the boundary), and
            every pair (line) and volume (dot) whose difference is not
            the printed digits, colored by label

FILES

  run_parity_tests.sh    runner (work/, logs/)
  check_parity.py        checks, pictures, summary.html
  make_parity_gold.sh    makes LaGriT's .stor files (needs LaGriT)
  make_utm_mesh.py       the UTM-coordinate mesh
  cases.txt              name | mesh | what it does
  inputs/                LaGriT's .stor files, the deck (gold.lgi), its
                         screen output (gold.out), LAGRIT_VERSION, and
                         the meshes copied from LaGriT (BSD-3, LANL
                         LA-CC-15-069)
